<script lang="ts">
	import { examples } from '../../utils/examples'

	const open = signal(false)
	const mode = signal<'lucide:moon' | 'lucide:sun'>('lucide:sun')
	const toggleMode = (): void => {
		mode.value = mode.value === 'lucide:sun' ? 'lucide:moon' : 'lucide:sun'
	}
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Icon"
		description="Iconify icons and your own SVGs, typed and inlined in the HTML at build time."
	>
		<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
		<div class="preview">
			<p>
				<UIIcon name="lucide:search" />
				Search the project
			</p>
			<UIButton variant="outline">
				<UIIcon
					name="lucide:trash-2"
					label="Delete"
				/>
			</UIButton>
		</div>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.icon" />
		<p>
			<code>UIIcon</code>
			writes an inline
			<code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>
			. Each literal name is resolved during the build with the collection package installed in the project: there are no runtime requests or CDN, and the bundle only carries the icons you use.
		</p>

		<h2 id="setup">Installation and collections</h2>
		<p>
			Install the module and each Iconify collection you want to use as
			<code>@iconify-json/&lt;collection&gt;</code>
			. The module is registered by its name and its options go in the
			<code>icon</code>
			key, typed in
			<code>meeko.config.ts</code>
			.
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.iconConfig" />
		<p>
			The available names form a TypeScript union that Meeko generates in
			<code>.meeko/types</code>
			: the editor completes
			<code>name="lucide:…"</code>
			, and a name that does not exist is a
			<code>meeko check</code>
			error with the closest suggestion. If the package of a configured collection is missing, the build prints the command to install it.
		</p>

		<h2 id="dynamic">Dynamic names</h2>
		<p>
			With
			<code>bind:name</code>
			, the literals of the expression are resolved at build time just like a fixed name. A value that does not appear in the code, such as one that comes from data, only works if it is in
			<code>icon.include</code>
			(or with
			<code>'collection:*'</code>
			, which includes the whole collection). Otherwise an empty
			<code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>
			is rendered and
			<code>meeko dev</code>
			warns in the console.
		</p>
		<div class="preview">
			<UIButton
				variant="secondary"
				on:click="() => (open.value = !open.value)"
			>
				<UIIcon
					bind:name="open.value ? 'lucide:x' : 'lucide:menu'"
					bind:label="open.value ? 'Close menu' : 'Open menu'"
				/>
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="secondary"
				on:click="toggleMode"
			>
				<UIIcon
					bind:name="mode.value"
					bind:label="mode.value === 'lucide:sun' ? 'Light mode' : 'Dark mode'"
				/>
			</UIButton>
		</div>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.iconDynamic" />

		<h2 id="local">Your own SVGs</h2>
		<p>
			Each file in
			<code>app/icons</code>
			(or in the folder of
			<code>icon.local</code>
			) is
			<code>local:&lt;name&gt;</code>
			. It is cleaned at build time:
			<code>&lt;script&gt;</code>
			,
			<code>&lt;style&gt;</code>
			, event handlers, inline styles and external references are removed, and a single-color icon switches to
			<code>currentColor</code>
			.
		</p>
		<div class="preview">
			<UIIcon
				name="local:paw"
				label="Meeko"
				size="1.5em"
			/>
		</div>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.iconLocal" />

		<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility, size and color</h2>
		<p>
			Without
			<code>label</code>
			, the icon is decorative:
			<code>aria-hidden="true"</code>
			and
			<code>focusable="false"</code>
			. With
			<code>label</code>
			, the
			<code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>
			gets
			<code>role="img"</code>
			and
			<code>aria-label</code>
			; use it when the icon is the only content of a button or a link.
		</p>
		<p>
			It is
			<code>1em</code>
			tall by default, so it follows the surrounding text, and it takes its color from
			<code>currentColor</code>
			. Width, height and fill are attributes, never inline styles: it works with a strict Content Security Policy.
		</p>
		<div class="preview">
			<UIIcon
				name="lucide:star"
				size="16px"
			/>
			<UIIcon
				name="lucide:star"
				size="24px"
			/>
			<UIIcon
				name="lucide:star"
				size="2.5em"
			/>
		</div>

		<h2 id="api">API</h2>
		<DocsApi
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'name', type: 'IconName', description: 'Icon: collection:icon or local:name. A literal is resolved at build time.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Accessible text. Without it, the icon is decorative.' },
				{ name: 'size', type: 'string', default: 'icon.size (1em)', description: 'Height, a CSS length. The width follows the proportion of the icon.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes of the svg.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h3 id="options">Module options</h3>
		<DocsApi
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'collections', type: 'string[]', default: '[]', description: 'Iconify collections; each one, the @iconify-json/<collection> package of the project.' },
				{ name: 'include', type: 'IconInclude[]', default: '[]', description: 'Icons for dynamic names, or collection:* for a whole one.' },
				{ name: 'local', type: 'string | false', default: 'app/icons if it exists', description: 'Folder of your own SVGs.' },
				{ name: 'size', type: 'string', default: '1em', description: 'Default height of the icons.' },
			]"
		/>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
